MonteCarloTree

MonteCarloNode:
player color
pointer to parent
list of pointers to children
traversal counter
win counter

class StudentAI():

    def __init__(self,col,row,p):
        self.col = col
        self.row = row
        self.p = p
        self.board = Board(col,row,p)
        self.board.initialize_game()
        self.color = ''
        self.opponent = {1:2,2:1}
        self.color = 2
        
        self.root = MCTSNode(self.board, None, None, None)
        #TODO self.time_limit
        
    def get_move(self, move):
        if len(move) != 0:
            self.board.make_move(move, self.opponent[self.color])
            #TODO set root node color
        else:
            self.color = 1  # if no enemy move, that means we're first (color = 1)
        #TODO build tree, choose move
            
            
    def build_tree(self, c, depth):
        start_time = time.time()
        finished = False
        while not finished and (time.time() - start_time < self.time_limit):
            finished = self.root.select(c, depth)


class MCTSNode():
    def __init__(self, board, move = None, color, parent = None):
        self.board = board
        self.move = move
        self.turn = len(self.board.saved_move)
        self.color = color
        self.parent = parent
        self.children = []
        self.unexplored = []
        self.wins = 0
        self.visits = 0
        self.is_terminal = False

    def uct_value(self, c):
        return self.wins/self.visits + c*math.sqrt(math.log(self.parent.visits)/self.visits)

    def reset(self):
        counter = len(self.board.saved_moves) - self.turn
        for i in range(counter):
            self.board.undo()
        
    def select(self, c, depth)
        # TODO: UPDATE BOARD PER MOVE
        # STOP IF WIN STATE SELECTED
        '''
        select recursively till max depth or no children found
        if max depth, finished = True
        if no children, call exp_and_sim and restart from root
        case where no children: expansion and simulation
        '''
        if self.children.empty():
            # add children to queue and simulate
            # get all possible moves, make new child nodes
            # backpropagate and update all node counters
            # TODO
            self.exp_and_sim()
            return False
        else:
            if depth > 0: # max depth hasn't been reached: traverse recursively
                max_child = max(self.children, key=lambda child: child.uct_value(c)) # chooses the first max
                return max_child.select(c, depth - 1)
            return True # max depth traversed without missing children = finished
    
    def expand(self)
        win_status = self.board.is_win(self.color)
        if win_status != 0:
            self.is_terminal = True
            self.backpropagate(win_status)
            return
        
        moves = self.board.get_all_possible_moves(self.color)
        legal_moves = [m for checker_moves in moves for m in checker_moves]
        
        if not legal_moves:
            
        self.simulate()
        self.backpropagate()
            
        
        self.backpropagate()
    
    def backpropagate(self, winner):
    	node = self
      while node is not None:
          node.visits += 1
          if node.parent is not None:
              mover = node.parent.color
              if winner == mover:
                  node.wins += 1
              elif winner == -1:
                  node.wins += 0.5
          node = node.parent
        
    
        
    def return_best_move(self):
        for child in self.children:
            return max(self.children.move, key=lambda child: child.uct_value(c))


Functions:
return uct done
create node
recursive delete node (not needed in python)

When opponent chooses move,
1. locate child node for resulting state
2. separate it from original tree
3. delete original tree
4. set child node as root
5. build rest of tree

Current state (root)
Possible moves this turn.... (rollouts (1st iter/skipped potentially), UCT (2nd iter), return best UCT (4th iter)) b
Possible opponent moves.... (new root) (rollouts (2nd iter), UCT (3rd iter)) ab
Possible moves for us to choose from next turn.... (rollouts (3rd iter), UCT(4th iter/final)) a^2b
if a = 1, total work is O(b); set exploration parameter(c) to sqrt(2)?

MCTS Tree building:

Selection:
you are on this current node
to check if you've run rollouts on children, check if child list is empty
if child list is not empty, then run UCT because you have wins and traversal counts already

Expansion and Simulation:
if child list is empty, you add all children to frontier (queue) and simulate rollouts (multithreading???)

Backpropagation:
update wins and traversal for children (could be done inside simulation portion)
we update wins and traversal for current node.  now you can do UCT

